<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">East Lothian</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothian">Lothian</a> is a council area of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a> on the southern shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firth-of-forth">Firth of Forth</a>, with Haddington as its historic county town. It contains the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> hillfort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/traprain-law">Traprain Law</a>, a centre of the Votadini, and the site of the Battle of Prestonpans of 1745.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/east-lothian.jpg" alt="East Lothian" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:East_Lothian_in_Scotland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
